{"t":"Oskayaat","s":"oskayaat-145d4","k":"local","i":"assets/wiki/Gerib_b20e04.gif","q":2,"html":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" dir=\"ltr\" lang=\"en\"><aside class=\"portable-infobox pi-background pi-border-color pi-theme-twbox pi-layout-default\" role=\"region\">\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-item-spacing pi-title pi-secondary-background\" data-source=\"name\">Oskayaat</h2>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">General Properties</h2>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"ruler\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Ruled by</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Unknown</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"population\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Population</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Unknown</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"organization\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Organizations</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Unknown</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"near\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Nearby places</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"#/wiki/Chor\">Chor</a>, <a href=\"#/wiki/Ankrahmun\">Ankrahmun</a></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<table class=\"pi-horizontal-group\">\n<caption class=\"pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-secondary-background pi-item-spacing\">Local</caption>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th class=\"pi-horizontal-group-item pi-data-label pi-secondary-font pi-border-color pi-item-spacing\" data-source=\"implemented\">Hunting Places</th>\n<th class=\"pi-horizontal-group-item pi-data-label pi-secondary-font pi-border-color pi-item-spacing\" data-source=\"implemented\">Quests</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pi-horizontal-group-item pi-data-value pi-font pi-border-color pi-item-spacing\" data-source=\"implemented\"><div class=\"geo-toc\"><ul><li><a href=\"#/wiki/Murky%20Caverns\">Murky Caverns</a></li><li><a href=\"#/wiki/Oskayaat%20Undercity\">Oskayaat Undercity</a></li></ul></div></td>\n<td class=\"pi-horizontal-group-item pi-data-value pi-font pi-border-color pi-item-spacing\" data-source=\"implemented\"><div class=\"geo-toc\"><ul><li><a href=\"#/quest/grimvale-quest\">Grimvale Quest</a></li><li><a href=\"#/quest/shards-of-a-broken-moon-quest\">Shards of a Broken Moon Quest</a></li></ul></div></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Other Properties</h2>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"implemented\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Version</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><span class=\"implementation-date\">13.20.13560<br/>July 10, 2023<br/>Summer Update 2023</span></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><p>\t    See also: Locations <span class=\"explained\">Help</span></p></nav>\n</aside>\n<p><br/>\n<b>Oskayaat</b> is an enchanting island located to the south of <a href=\"#/wiki/Chor\">Chor</a> and <a href=\"#/wiki/Ankrahmun\">Ankrahmun</a>, geographically divided into two distinct regions. Its mesmerizing landscape comprises a lush jungle in the west and an expansive steppe in the east, separated by a magnificent central mountain range. Within these mountains lies the beautiful city of Oska, serving as a testament to the architectural prowess of the Oskayaans and their deep connection with the land. To the southeast, on a smaller island, a captivating volcano occasionally exhibits its fiery spectacle.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"w-Geography\">Geography</span></h2>\n<p>The island's western region is characterized by a dense jungle, abundant with diverse flora and fauna, while the eastern side boasts vast open plains offering breathtaking vistas. The central mountain range not only divides the island into contrasting environments of arid east and humid, overgrown west but also holds the magnificent city of Oska amidst its peaks. The smaller southeastern island, with its active volcano, adds an extra element of awe and wonder to Oskayaat's already captivating scenery.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"w-Culture_and_Civilization\">Culture and Civilization</span></h2>\n<p>Oskayaat's inhabitants are known for their highly developed civilization, which celebrates art, beauty, and a rich cultural heritage. The Oskayaans possess a deep understanding of history, mythology, and philosophy, with a profound respect for ancient knowledge and traditions. Their religious and spiritual beliefs are at the core of their lives, reflecting a peaceful and respectful society. In the past, they worshipped Suon, the sun god, and Amati, the moon goddess, equally. Over time, their devotion shifted, giving more prominence to the sun as the source of life and creation, while the moon's significance waned, representing the cycle of life.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"w-The_Curse_of_the_Werecreatures\">The Curse of the Werecreatures</span></h2>\n<p>Oskayaat's tranquil existence was once shattered by a malevolent curse that afflicted its people, turning them into fearsome <a href=\"#/wiki/Lycanthropes\">werecreatures</a> during specific moon phases. In an extraordinary twist, the Oskayaans transformed into <a href=\"#/wiki/Weretiger\">weretigers</a>, <a href=\"#/wiki/Werepanther\">werepanthers</a>, and <a href=\"#/wiki/Werecrocodile\">werecrocodiles</a>, reflecting the island's unique and diverse wildlife. The sudden dominance of the moon during the curse's onset plunged the island into chaos, spreading madness and mayhem among its inhabitants.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"w-A_Tale_of_Redemption\">A Tale of Redemption</span></h2>\n<p>Amidst the turmoil, a group of valiant adventurers stepped forward, determined to save Oskayaat from impending doom. Through their bravery, they managed to bring the curse under control, guiding the people to embrace their werecreature identities. Thus, Oskayaat became a sanctuary for werecreatures, where trade, craftsmanship, and a vibrant way of life continued to flourish despite the curse's presence.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"w-The_Road_to_Recovery\">The Road to Recovery</span></h2>\n<p>The initial impact of the curse left its mark on the city of Oska, necessitating significant restoration efforts to reclaim the island's former glory. Undeterred, the resilient inhabitants of Oskayaat united to repair the damages and revive their cherished homeland, showcasing their unwavering spirit and determination.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"w-Legacy_and_Significance\">Legacy and Significance</span></h2>\n<p>Oskayaat's captivating tale of transformation and redemption continues to inspire numerous legends and stories, attracting adventurers and scholars eager to unravel its mysteries. The harmony between the werecreatures and their island home stands as a symbol of resilience and the ability to triumph over adversity. While the sun holds its rightful place in Oskayaat's cultural practices, the moon remains a part of their identity, carrying the memory of the curse and the island's remarkable journey towards restoration and greatness.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"w-Epilogue\">Epilogue</span></h2>\n<p>With its breathtaking landscapes and rich cultural heritage, Oskayaat remains a captivating destination that weaves a tapestry of history, courage, and redemption, leaving visitors and locals alike enthralled by its enchanting allure.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"w-NPCs\">NPCs</span></h2>\n<h3 style=\"font-weight:bold;\"><span id=\"w-Oskayaat_NPCs_.286_NPCs.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"w-Oskayaat_NPCs_(6_NPCs)\">Oskayaat NPCs (6 NPCs)</span></h3>\n<table class=\"wikitable sortable full-width\" style=\"text-align:center;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Name\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>Job\n</th>\n<th>Buy/Sell\n</th>\n<th>Location\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"\"><a href=\"#/wiki/Gerib\">Gerib</a>\n</td>\n<td class=\"npc-animation\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"#/wiki/Gerib\"><img alt=\"Gerib\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"64\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Gerib_b20e04.gif\" width=\"64\"/></a></span>\n</td>\n<td>Postman\n</td>\n<td><span class=\"yes-tick\" title=\"Yes\">✓</span>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:left;\">\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"\"><a href=\"#/wiki/Kiru\">Kiru</a>\n</td>\n<td class=\"npc-animation\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"#/wiki/Kiru\"><img alt=\"Kiru\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"64\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Kiru_ee36e6.gif\" width=\"64\"/></a></span>\n</td>\n<td>Unknown.\n</td>\n<td><span class=\"yes-tick\" title=\"Yes\">✓</span>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:left;\">\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"\"><a href=\"#/wiki/Niral\">Niral</a>\n</td>\n<td class=\"npc-animation\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"#/wiki/Niral\"><img alt=\"Niral\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"64\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Niral_096ecf.gif\" width=\"64\"/></a></span>\n</td>\n<td>Cleric\n</td>\n<td><span class=\"no-cross\" title=\"No\">✗</span>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:left;\">\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"\"><a href=\"#/wiki/Tamru\">Tamru</a>\n</td>\n<td class=\"npc-animation\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"#/wiki/Tamru\"><img alt=\"Tamru\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"64\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Tamru_eecae7.gif\" width=\"64\"/></a></span>\n